SSupplemental Collaboration & Co‑Ownership Terms for the Royal Archer Project
Copyright (c) 2026 Galina B. Nelson

This document supplements the MIT License included in this repository.
It does not replace or limit the MIT License.
Instead, it establishes additional terms for contributors who wish to 
collaborate on the long‑term development of the Royal Archer platform 
and potentially participate in future co‑ownership of the editorial studio, 
digital tools, or related services.

1. Original Ownership
1.1. All code, text, designs, documentation, branding, and creative assets 
present in this repository prior to any third‑party contributions are the 
exclusive intellectual property of Galina B. Nelson.
1.2. Publishing this repository under the MIT License does not transfer
ownership of the original work or the Royal Archer brand.

2. Contributor License Grant
2.1. By submitting a pull request or any other contribution (“Contribution”), 
the contributor grants Galina B. Nelson a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, 
royalty‑free license to use, modify, distribute, and incorporate the Contribution
into the project and any future commercial or non‑commercial versions.
2.2. Contributors retain copyright to their own Contributions.

3. Contributor Certification
By contributing, each contributor confirms that:

the Contribution is their original work

they have the legal right to license it

it does not infringe on any third‑party rights

it is provided under the MIT License and these supplemental terms

This protects both the contributor and the project.

4. Pathway to Future Co‑Ownership
4.1. Contributing to this repository does not automatically grant ownership, 
equity, or revenue share in Royal Archer or any related platform.
4.2. Contributors may become co‑owners only through a separate written 
agreement signed by all existing owners.
4.3. Considerations for co‑ownership may include:

consistent, meaningful contributions

editorial, technical, or educational leadership

long‑term commitment to the project

alignment with Royal Archer’s mission and values

ethical and collaborative behavior

4.4. No contributor may claim co‑ownership based solely on code or content contributions.

5. Project Governance
5.1. Until a formal co‑ownership agreement is created, all major decisions regarding project
direction, editorial standards, platform architecture, and governance are made by the project owner (Galina B. Nelson).
5.2. Contributors agree to follow the project’s Code of Conduct and collaboration guidelines.

6. Branding, Creative Assets, and Editorial Identity
6.1. All branding elements—including the Royal Archer name, logo, editorial voice, written 
content, course materials, and creative assets—are not covered by the MIT License and remain 
the exclusive property of Galina B. Nelson unless otherwise stated.
6.2. Contributors may not use the Royal Archer brand for independent commercial purposes without written permission.
6.3. Any new creative assets contributed to the project must align with the studio’s tone, values, and editorial standards.

7. Commercial Use of the Future Platform
7.1. The open‑source code in this repository may be used freely under the MIT License.
7.2. The official Royal Archer platform, including editorial services, courses,
digital tools, and community features, may operate under separate commercial terms.
7.3. Contributors who become co‑owners will participate in revenue‑sharing and 
decision‑making according to a future written agreement.

8. Warranty Disclaimer
This Addendum does not modify the MIT License warranty disclaimer.
The software is provided “as is”, without warranty of any kind.

9. Relationship to the MIT License
9.1. In the event of any conflict between this Addendum and the MIT License, 
the MIT License governs the use of the code.
9.2. These supplemental terms govern collaboration, contributions, and 
future co‑ownership, not the licensing of the code itself.
